      "side": 1,
      "message": "Don\u0027t worry, Chrome recommends this approach: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/HEAD/docs/static_initializers.md#Removing-Static-Initializers\n\nAnd Google3 allows it:\nhttp://go/cstyle#common_patterns \"If all else fails, you can create an object dynamically and never delete it by using gtl::NoDestructor.\"\n\nI\u0027d be totally fine with a different version that does this without involving `sk_sp\u003c\u003e` in the static, but I don\u0027t understand how you dodge `~sk_sp` unreffing and deleting the object once the first caller is done with it, so I\u0027d ask you to put that together for me. I\u0027ll +1 it if it works!",
